  "description": "DEWYIR crystallizes in the cubic crystal system with space group P 21 3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C390 H264 Eu12 O120 P18,8(C2 H6 O1),7(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu5 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu6 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu7 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu8 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu9 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu10 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu11 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu12 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 4.791-4.988 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 138.40-149.11°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Eu12(C2O4)9(R-BNP)18(EtOH)6(H2O)6·8EtOH·7H2O (C406H316Eu12O135P18; CCDC formula C390H264Eu12O120P18·8EtOH·7H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
